/E ([0014]   According to the embodiment of the present invention, the mechanism is kinematically constrained. It means that the mechanism cannot open or close more than the set limit by the dimension of its bars. This is essential as to prevent any overshoot of linkages. Its it specially essential in the case of return stroke when the hook takes its initial position with high velocity. If the mechanism is not constrained kinematically then in the aforesaid scenario the hook might cross its desired location because of its inertia and thus a singularity is observed. To prevent this singularity, the initiation bar and the supporting bar are coupled in a manner such that during the maximum desired extension their central axis align and any further actuation would violate the geometry. Moreover, the revolute joint between the initiation bar and the supporting bar is not kept on the central axis, but rather kept in the side opposite to the hook side, so as to constraint the mechanism before the hook can overshoot. In case of the 6 bar )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
