/E ([0026] We can see the various phases of hook movement are clearly represented in Figure 10\(a\). Initial actuation of the the cutter results in the hooking phase, where the hooks rotates very fast, which is clearly shown as points are far apart. In the next pulling the hook pulls the pedicel inside to cut which is clearly represented. In the last holding phase the speed decreases and the hook position is almost static, which is shown by dark region in the end as the points are very close to each other. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [69]
